 Democratic fraud scandal, could tighten this into Lean D territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tina Smith (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's open Senate seat features Democrat Peggy Flanagan against Republican Michele Tafoya, with incumbent Tina Smith retiring. The state leans Democratic by about three points on partisanship, and every recent poll shows Flanagan ahead, typically by three to four points. Expert raters mostly call the race Likely or Lean Democratic, though a few see it as closer.\n\nFlanagan has outraised Tafoya and drawn heavy outside spending against her, a sign Republicans view the seat as winnable. Prediction markets put her chances near 87%. The forecast expects a Flanagan win by roughly five points, with meaningful uncertainty given the narrow polling lead and an unsettled national environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8725, "margin": 5.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8131, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8217, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.784, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7719, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7956, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7935, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7758, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8073, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7878, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7863, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.738, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7059, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7067, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8031, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7655, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7895, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.8034, "margin": 5.0}